### Post 'Hello!" - answers 201 with the persisted message, its id and detected language
POST http://localhost:8080/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "Hello!"
}

### Post "Bonjour!"

POST http://localhost:8080/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "Bonjour!"
}

### Post "Privet!"

POST http://localhost:8080/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "Privet!"
}

### Get all the messages
GET http://localhost:8080/

### Blank text is rejected with 400 and an error body carrying the request id
POST http://localhost:8080/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "  "
}

### Reuse a known request id, to grep it straight out of `docker compose logs`
POST http://localhost:8080/
Content-Type: application/json
X-Request-Id: my-trace

{
  "text": "Traceable!"
}

### Longer text detects more reliably than a one-word greeting
POST http://localhost:8080/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "Bonjour mon ami, comment vas-tu aujourd'hui ?"
}
